WEBVTT

00:00.824 --> 00:04.150
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.206 --> 00:07.304
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.338 --> 00:10.999
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.033 --> 00:13.997
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.031 --> 00:17.396
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.430 --> 00:20.660
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.694 --> 00:22.159
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.193 --> 00:23.723
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.757 --> 00:26.136
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.622 --> 00:38.684
Ah, Smitty's Steakhouse.

00:38.919 --> 00:41.284
You know, this was the
fanciest restaurant in Quahog

00:41.318 --> 00:44.046
when I was a kid.
The ladies' room has a big space

00:44.081 --> 00:46.447
with chairs in it, like a living
room, before you get back

00:46.481 --> 00:47.712
to where the crappers are.

00:47.746 --> 00:49.545
Good evening and
welcome to Smitty's.

00:49.579 --> 00:51.542
I'll be back with
martinis for Mom and Dad,

00:51.576 --> 00:54.241
and for you kids,
some martinis.

00:54.276 --> 00:55.906
Dad, can you pass
the bread?

00:55.940 --> 00:58.339
Sure. But don't forget
the butter that looks like

00:58.373 --> 01:01.637
decorative bathroom soaps and
is impossible to smear.

01:04.701 --> 01:08.331
Thanks, Dad!
This really ruins it!

01:08.365 --> 01:10.065
What will you
be having, sir?

01:10.099 --> 01:12.628
Yes, I'll have what I had last
time: pheasant on the glass.

01:12.662 --> 01:14.528
Don't you mean
"pheasant under glass"?

01:14.562 --> 01:15.793
Nope.

01:17.891 --> 01:21.887
Yeah. Now turn around
and lay an egg on the glass.

01:24.055 --> 01:26.284
Aw, yeah.

01:26.319 --> 01:30.015
I defy you to tell me
exactly what's wrong with this.

01:33.747 --> 01:36.147
Oh, Peter, look.
You can put your business card

01:36.181 --> 01:38.143
in this bowl
and maybe win a free lunch.

01:38.177 --> 01:39.978
I don't have a
business card.

01:40.011 --> 01:42.174
And I think
you knew that.

01:42.208 --> 01:43.841
I hope you enjoyed
your meal, sir.

01:43.876 --> 01:46.338
May I offer you a toothpick?
Oh, I-I don't know.

01:46.372 --> 01:48.338
We've already spent
a lot of money in here tonight.

01:48.372 --> 01:51.404
No, sir, it-it's free.

01:53.036 --> 01:55.464
Oh!

01:58.631 --> 02:00.597
Peter, that's not how
you use a toothpick.

02:00.631 --> 02:02.094
You pick your teeth
with it.

02:02.129 --> 02:04.661
I cannot believe I have
to explain this to you.

02:04.695 --> 02:07.690
There are gaps in my knowledge.
This is hardly news.

02:09.358 --> 02:11.088
Wow, this is awesome!

02:11.123 --> 02:13.954
This is like
I'm having a whole second meal!

02:15.619 --> 02:18.584
Man, this just feels right.

02:18.618 --> 02:21.649
That's it. From here on out, I
am about all things toothpick.

02:21.683 --> 02:24.145
I'm gonna go everywhere with
it, always be chewin' on it,

02:24.179 --> 02:25.913
#-and start all my
sentences with,

02:25.947 --> 02:27.478
"All right, here's
what you're gonna do."

02:27.512 --> 02:29.477
Excuse me, we're
from out of town.

02:29.511 --> 02:32.107
Where do people go to listen
to live music around here?

02:32.141 --> 02:34.108
I'll handle this. All right,
here's what you're gonna do:

02:34.141 --> 02:35.938
skip the live music.
Get yourself a room

02:35.972 --> 02:38.105
over at the Wickford Marina.
Take her out on a balcony,

02:38.139 --> 02:40.335
point to any boat in the harbor,
and tell her it's yours.

02:40.370 --> 02:42.435
Now, you got rubbers?
Now that I'm a toothpick guy,

02:42.470 --> 02:44.432
I call 'em rubbers. Or you could
just pull the hose out

02:44.466 --> 02:45.933
of the bucket
and let it spray free.

02:45.967 --> 02:49.029
I've had a vasectomy.

02:51.862 --> 02:54.493
Chris, now that I'm a toothpick
guy, it's my job to sit

02:54.527 --> 02:56.491
on a BMX bike
outside the rec center

02:56.525 --> 02:58.924
and ask every kid
if they're the new kid.

02:58.958 --> 03:00.921
Hey. You the new kid?

03:00.955 --> 03:02.589
Why?
Never mind why.

03:02.623 --> 03:05.584
Got any cool toys?
Uh, I got an Xbox.

03:05.619 --> 03:08.150
How about you?
I got a Barbie with a wiener on it.

03:08.185 --> 03:11.149
Took a thumb from a G.I. Joe,
put it on with superglue.

03:11.184 --> 03:13.412
Looks pretty real.
Real enough, anyways.

03:13.447 --> 03:15.479
Does the job.
Does what job?

03:15.513 --> 03:18.076
You get it. My family
moves around a lot

03:18.110 --> 03:19.743
'cause I do stuff like this.

03:19.777 --> 03:21.242
Um... okay.

03:21.276 --> 03:23.138
I got to go now.
You sure you don't want

03:23.176 --> 03:25.073
to come over and pull
on my cat's nipples?

03:25.107 --> 03:28.437
We can do anything,
'cause my mom has two jobs.

03:30.468 --> 03:31.935
All right,
I'm off to the fish market.

03:31.970 --> 03:33.533
What? Why?

03:33.567 --> 03:35.597
Well, the most intimidating
people are toothpick guys

03:35.631 --> 03:37.763
who work at seafood counters
and make people uncomfortable

03:37.798 --> 03:39.694
for not knowing
about fish.

03:39.728 --> 03:41.128
What's good here?
It's all good.

03:41.163 --> 03:42.627
What's the freshest?
It's all fresh.

03:42.660 --> 03:43.892
How 'bout the halibut?
Is it gamey?

03:43.915 --> 03:44.826
Gamey?

03:44.827 --> 03:47.056
I mean, you know, is it fishy?
It's all fish.

03:47.090 --> 03:49.789
Is there a special way to prepare it?
I'd cook it up.

03:49.823 --> 03:51.387
W-Well, what's
the best fish here?

03:51.421 --> 03:52.555
What's your favorite fish?

03:52.590 --> 03:55.451
I don't eat fish.
I only like spaghetti.

04:00.015 --> 04:02.214
Ugh, when are you gonna
get rid of that toothpick?

04:02.248 --> 04:04.710
It's disgusting,
and it's starting to smell.

04:04.744 --> 04:06.702
Why would I give it up?
It's gettin' me tons of tail.

04:06.726 --> 04:07.809
What?

04:07.810 --> 04:11.241
And check this out.
The rare triple toothpick flip.

04:16.537 --> 04:18.736
Oh, my God,
are you all right?

04:18.771 --> 04:20.567
No, I swallowed it!

04:20.601 --> 04:22.334
My toothpick! It's gone!

04:22.368 --> 04:24.398
Damn it! I'm gonna need
you to put that large

04:24.432 --> 04:26.032
two-handed colander
over the toilet.

04:26.066 --> 04:28.029
Peter, that was
a wedding present from my aunt.

04:28.063 --> 04:29.460
Well, let's use
the ice cream maker!

04:29.495 --> 04:30.595
We've never used it once!

04:30.629 --> 04:33.591
Calm down. You can always get
another toothpick.

04:33.625 --> 04:35.193
Oh, my God, you're right!

04:35.226 --> 04:36.690
Lois, we got to drive
to Smitty's right now

04:36.724 --> 04:39.089
and get one.
Now? But we told Chris

04:39.124 --> 04:41.852
we'd be there
when he wakes up from surgery.

04:43.188 --> 04:45.650
All right, we were able
to fix your hernia,

04:45.684 --> 04:48.049
but you've got to stop lifting
sewer hole covers.

04:48.083 --> 04:49.814
But the Ninja Turtles
live down there.

04:49.848 --> 04:51.048
I'm friends with them.

04:51.082 --> 04:53.145
Hey, fat ass,
I brought you flowers.

04:53.180 --> 04:55.877
But stay out of the sewers!
We're trying to work down there.

04:55.912 --> 04:58.175
Thanks, Donatello!

04:59.910 --> 05:01.307
Oh, thank God!

05:01.341 --> 05:03.171
Quick, we need
another toothpick!

05:03.205 --> 05:06.602
Thank you, Maurice.

05:15.630 --> 05:18.262
Just get your toothpick
and let's get out of here.

05:18.296 --> 05:19.560
Ugh. No, thanks.

05:19.594 --> 05:21.993
That old lady has ruined
toothpicks for me.

05:22.027 --> 05:24.226
Just like how Meg
ruined broccoli.

05:24.261 --> 05:26.223
Hey, Meg, look,
they're little trees!

05:26.258 --> 05:27.488
No, they're not.

05:27.523 --> 05:29.721
They're not?!

05:29.755 --> 05:32.151
Hey, Peter!

05:32.185 --> 05:34.817
Oh, look, there's Quagmire
and his transgendered mother,

05:34.851 --> 05:38.016
which is now great.

05:38.050 --> 05:39.380
Hey, Quagmire. Hey, Ida.

05:39.414 --> 05:41.014
I didn't know
you liked Smitty's.

05:41.048 --> 05:42.679
Oh, yeah, I've been coming here
for ages.

05:42.714 --> 05:44.443
They even named a sandwich
after me.

05:44.477 --> 05:46.843
It's an inside-out hot dog
slathered in ketchup.

05:46.877 --> 05:48.974
Please, please
join us.

05:49.008 --> 05:51.972
Oh, we wouldn't want
to interrupt your brave dinner.

05:52.006 --> 05:53.639
Nonsense, we're happy
to have you.

05:53.673 --> 05:55.238
All right,
but we already ate dinner,

05:55.272 --> 05:58.802
so maybe just an iceberg wedge,
a steak, and some sides.

05:58.836 --> 06:01.165
And then I said something random
that suggested

06:01.199 --> 06:02.832
a whole crazy story!

06:05.330 --> 06:07.295
Oh, God, that's
hilarious, Lois.

06:07.330 --> 06:09.127
I could listen to
you talk all night.

06:09.161 --> 06:11.726
Yeah, but we got to get going.
Carter's our babysitter,

06:11.761 --> 06:14.891
and if he's with the kids too
long, they start sayin' racisms.

06:14.925 --> 06:16.888
Aw, I wish the fun didn't have
to end.

06:16.922 --> 06:19.454
I always enjoy spending time
with you two.

06:19.489 --> 06:21.252
Well, why don't you
come over tomorrow?

06:21.286 --> 06:24.584
We'll fire up the grill and have
the gang over for a cookout.

06:24.618 --> 06:26.983
Well, that sounds wonderful.
Well, great, we'll be there!

06:27.017 --> 06:28.914
Hey, before you two
leave, let's take a photo.

06:28.949 --> 06:31.247
Yeah! Selfie!

06:31.281 --> 06:33.643
I just learned that word.

06:36.643 --> 06:39.106
Perfect! Well, good
night, you guys.

06:39.140 --> 06:41.439
See you tomorrow,
hashtags!

06:41.474 --> 06:43.805
You're not doin'
that right.

06:47.301 --> 06:49.700
Boy, that Lois is really
something, isn't she?

06:49.734 --> 06:52.599
Yeah. Peter's
a lucky guy.

06:52.633 --> 06:54.197
Glenn, do you...

06:54.231 --> 06:56.597
do you have feelings for her?

06:56.630 --> 06:58.927
- What?
- No.

06:58.961 --> 07:00.361
A mother always knows.

07:00.395 --> 07:02.357
You like to play the
field, but, deep down,

07:02.392 --> 07:05.124
you really wish you had a
woman like Lois, don't you?

07:05.158 --> 07:06.954
<i>No, I don't want a woman
like Lois.</i>

07:06.988 --> 07:08.788
I want Lois.

07:08.823 --> 07:11.118
She's perfect.
I've loved her for years.

07:11.152 --> 07:13.617
She's warm and kind
and beautiful.

07:13.652 --> 07:16.081
I've never been so in love
with anyone.

07:16.115 --> 07:17.915
Glenn, that's
very sweet,

07:17.949 --> 07:20.411
but you're talking about
your best friend's wife.

07:20.446 --> 07:22.012
I know, I know.
It's wrong.

07:22.046 --> 07:23.410
And Peter's
a good friend.

07:23.445 --> 07:25.344
Not like Cleveland.

07:25.379 --> 07:27.407
Hey, I got two
of these phone books.

07:27.442 --> 07:29.006
Didn't know
if you wanted one.

07:29.040 --> 07:31.172
Hey, how long
have we known each other?

07:31.206 --> 07:35.170
Long time. And yet we've never
discussed mothers' maiden names,

07:35.204 --> 07:38.401
the names of old pets,
high school mascots,

07:38.436 --> 07:40.831
favorite teachers.
Heck, I don't even know

07:40.865 --> 07:42.832
the last four digits
of your Social.

07:42.866 --> 07:44.662
Cleveland, do you need
to borrow some money?

07:44.697 --> 07:46.678
I do!
They're gonna kill Donna!

07:46.679 --> 07:47.314
Really?

07:47.338 --> 07:49.639
No. I just want
to buy a man's fur coat.

07:49.925 --> 07:51.692
Get out of here.

07:54.459 --> 07:56.188
Hey, Peter,

07:56.222 --> 07:58.019
I had an extra
phone book, and I...

07:58.054 --> 08:00.353
I'm not buyin' you that coat!

08:06.781 --> 08:08.980
Huh? Who? What?

08:09.014 --> 08:10.980
Yeah, what? What? Which
doggy in what window?

08:11.014 --> 08:12.644
So, how'd everything go?

08:12.679 --> 08:14.475
Hard to tell. I was
coughing the whole time.

08:14.510 --> 08:16.475
By the way, I couldn't figure
out how to use your oven,

08:16.510 --> 08:18.206
so I destroyed it
in a blind rage.

08:18.241 --> 08:20.006
Well, good night.

08:20.041 --> 08:24.004
Ooh, after that steak, I got
to go lay down on the toilet.

08:25.330 --> 08:27.232
Huh. Looks like I got
a couple of messages.

08:27.870 --> 08:29.500
Uh, Dad? Dad?

08:29.534 --> 08:31.330
Grandpa's going nuts
on the oven.

08:31.364 --> 08:32.564
Can you come home quick?

08:32.599 --> 08:34.063
Who the hell is that?

08:34.097 --> 08:36.329
Huh. There's one from Quagmire.

08:37.500 --> 08:39.502
Huh, must've pocket-dialed me
again.

08:39.526 --> 08:41.991
I want Lois. She's perfect.

08:42.026 --> 08:43.555
I've loved her for years.

08:43.590 --> 08:46.154
She's warm and kind
and beautiful.

08:46.188 --> 08:48.152
I've never been so in love
with anyone.

08:48.186 --> 08:50.152
Oh, my God.

08:50.186 --> 08:52.382
Quagmire's in love with my wife?

08:52.416 --> 08:54.217
Hello?

08:54.251 --> 08:56.446
Peter, I'm having troubles
on the toilet.

08:56.481 --> 08:57.714
Bring the ice cream maker.

09:04.018 --> 09:05.984
Brian, there's somethin' I
got to talk to you about.

09:06.018 --> 09:08.547
Quagmire pocket-dialed
me last night.

09:08.581 --> 09:10.647
You got to hear this.

09:10.682 --> 09:12.811
I want Lois. She's perfect.

09:12.845 --> 09:15.311
I've loved her for years.
Oh, my God!

09:15.345 --> 09:17.308
He's in love
with Lois?

09:17.342 --> 09:18.975
Yeah, and if you keep
listenin', you can hear

09:19.009 --> 09:21.505
a Puerto Rican busboy get
fired in the background.

09:21.539 --> 09:24.138
It's pretty funny. He cries.
But can you believe Quagmire?!

09:24.172 --> 09:25.802
Well, I guess
it's not that shocking.

09:25.836 --> 09:28.534
I mean, he has said 100 times
that he wants to bang Lois.

09:28.568 --> 09:30.701
No, no, no, that's just
Quagmire bein' a horndog.

09:30.735 --> 09:32.498
This is love.

09:32.532 --> 09:34.631
I don't know, I think you're making
too big a deal out of this.

09:34.666 --> 09:36.928
Too big a deal?! The guy's
been sitting next to me

09:36.963 --> 09:38.629
all these years,
acting like he's my friend,

09:38.664 --> 09:40.860
when all he really wants
is to be with my wife!

09:40.893 --> 09:42.590
Geez, calm down.
No, I'm telling you,

09:42.624 --> 09:44.657
he's gonna try to take
Lois away from me.

09:44.691 --> 09:46.621
You know what? I'm going
over there right now

09:46.656 --> 09:49.420
and hit him with a shovel, like
a white trash YouTube girl.

09:49.454 --> 09:50.685
Peter, wait, wait.
Listen.

09:50.719 --> 09:53.118
Delete that message
and pretend you never heard it.

09:53.152 --> 09:54.317
What? Why?

09:54.350 --> 09:56.017
Because you weren't meant
to hear it.

09:56.051 --> 09:58.846
If you act on this, all you'll
do is wreck your friendship

09:58.880 --> 10:00.680
and cause heartache
for everyone involved.

10:00.714 --> 10:01.967
What, so what am I supposed
to do, just ignore it?

10:01.991 --> 10:04.214
Yeah. Ignore it.
Like you do with the ghost

10:04.215 --> 10:06.858
of that colonial woman who
died falling down our stairs.

10:07.641 --> 10:11.738
I saw you
eat a crayon...

10:11.772 --> 10:14.104
It was purple.
I thought it was grape.

10:14.138 --> 10:16.236
Look, you've got to be
the bigger man.

10:16.271 --> 10:18.268
You got to just keep this
to yourself.

10:18.302 --> 10:20.301
Fine,
I won't say anything.

10:20.335 --> 10:22.431
Good. And don't be
passive-aggressive, either.

10:22.466 --> 10:25.264
Like one of those songs
in an old musical.

10:26.496 --> 10:28.492
♪ You're hideous ♪

10:28.526 --> 10:30.393
♪ To be without ♪

10:30.427 --> 10:32.057
♪ You're big and fat ♪

10:32.092 --> 10:33.824
♪ In the heart,
no doubt ♪

10:33.858 --> 10:35.589
♪ You're a horrible loss ♪

10:35.623 --> 10:37.655
♪ If you won't be my wife ♪

10:37.689 --> 10:39.885
♪ You're a raging,
continuous ♪

10:39.920 --> 10:43.018
♪ Love in my life... ♪

10:49.616 --> 10:51.045
Pretty good turnout
for this thing.

10:51.080 --> 10:53.443
<i>Oh, yeah, Mort
and Neil Goldman.</i>

10:53.476 --> 10:55.409
It's like Coachella.

10:58.908 --> 11:00.572
There's that son of a bitch!

11:00.607 --> 11:02.571
He's got some nerve
showing up here.

11:02.606 --> 11:04.436
Peter, remember what
we talked about.

11:04.470 --> 11:06.133
Look at them clouds
up there.

11:06.168 --> 11:07.734
Yeah, that one
look like Nathan.

11:07.768 --> 11:09.366
That one look
like Shawn.

11:09.400 --> 11:10.933
And there go Wanya
over there.

11:10.968 --> 11:13.928
How blessed are we to have
all them Boyz II Men

11:13.963 --> 11:16.195
just floating around
in the sky?

11:16.230 --> 11:17.626
Glenn! Ida!
You made it!

11:17.660 --> 11:19.460
Hey, Lois. I brought
the hamburger buns,

11:19.494 --> 11:20.725
like you wanted.

11:20.759 --> 11:22.057
I wasn't sure
what people like,

11:22.091 --> 11:24.623
so I got some with seeds on them
and some without.

11:24.657 --> 11:26.753
What does he mean
by that, "seeds"?

11:26.788 --> 11:28.587
Like semen?
Is that what he means?

11:28.621 --> 11:31.385
Semen on her buns.
Am I the only one hearing this?

11:31.420 --> 11:33.848
Get the hell away from my wife,
you scumbag!

11:33.883 --> 11:35.417
Peter, what are you
talking about?

11:35.451 --> 11:37.014
I'll tell you
what I'm talking about!

11:37.049 --> 11:38.213
I'm talking about this!

11:38.247 --> 11:39.846
Idea for a movie.

11:39.881 --> 11:43.342
<i>Fop Cop. It's a cop
who's, like, a fancy guy.</i>

11:43.376 --> 11:45.676
Nobody heard that!
None of you take that!

11:45.709 --> 11:47.942
What I meant to play was this.

11:47.976 --> 11:50.072
I want Lois. She's perfect.

11:50.105 --> 11:51.903
I've loved her for years.

11:51.938 --> 11:54.502
<i>Fop Cop.
That could work.</i>

11:54.536 --> 11:56.569
Glenn...
i-is this true?

11:56.603 --> 11:59.165
Wait a minute, how the hell'd you get
that recording, Peter?

11:59.200 --> 12:01.199
You pocket-dialed me,
you bastard!

12:01.233 --> 12:02.896
Peter, that was a
private conversation.

12:02.931 --> 12:06.228
That doesn't change the fact
that you want to steal my wife!

12:06.262 --> 12:08.258
Hey, get your
hands off me!

12:09.261 --> 12:10.824
Oh, my God!

12:10.859 --> 12:12.489
- Oh, come on, you two.
- Come on, man.

12:12.523 --> 12:13.723
Hey, what are y'all doing?
Someone stop him!

12:13.758 --> 12:14.922
Kill him, Dad!

12:14.956 --> 12:16.353
Murder him!

12:19.220 --> 12:20.850
That's it!
End of cookout!

12:20.884 --> 12:24.514
Get out of my house, and don't
ever speak to me again!

12:26.017 --> 12:27.979
Wow, that turned ugly fast.

12:28.014 --> 12:30.279
Just like my trip to Tampa Bay.

12:30.313 --> 12:33.441
Hey, city boy,
what's with the arm pants?

12:38.774 --> 12:40.870
I want Lois. She's perfect.

12:40.905 --> 12:42.571
I've loved her for years.

12:42.605 --> 12:44.668
You're still
listening to that thing?

12:44.702 --> 12:48.533
It's like, I can't even process
why he'd feel this way.

12:48.567 --> 12:50.865
Maybe... you know, maybe
play it one more time and...

12:50.900 --> 12:52.695
I can't believe this.

12:52.730 --> 12:54.528
I thought Quagmire
was my friend!

12:54.561 --> 12:56.527
Peter, it's not
that surprising.

12:56.561 --> 12:58.790
He's always had a
potent sex drive.

12:58.828 --> 13:01.390
Remember his
grandmother's funeral?

13:02.456 --> 13:04.489
Yeah, get it in there.

13:04.524 --> 13:06.153
<i>Oh, I wish this was
about sex.</i>

13:06.187 --> 13:08.752
If he was just home
busting one to his buddy's wife,

13:08.786 --> 13:10.483
hell, we've all done that.

13:10.518 --> 13:12.117
I've heard. Allegedly.

13:12.152 --> 13:14.548
But not often.
And never to Donna.

13:14.581 --> 13:17.280
Except when she wore those shiny
gold shorts to parent-teacher night.

13:17.314 --> 13:19.377
Oh, yeah, that
was hilarious.

13:19.411 --> 13:20.478
Yeah, that was...

13:20.513 --> 13:21.810
that was so tacky.

13:21.844 --> 13:24.543
But Quagmire actually has
feelings for you.

13:24.576 --> 13:27.704
I'm afraid he might take you
away from me.

13:27.738 --> 13:30.071
Peter, nobody's
taking me anywhere.

13:30.105 --> 13:31.835
<i>I love you.</i>

13:31.870 --> 13:32.870
Mmm.

13:32.904 --> 13:34.235
I love you, too, Lois.

13:34.269 --> 13:36.567
Hey, you ever heard
any of the other wives

13:36.602 --> 13:38.099
saying they're
attracted to me?

13:39.499 --> 13:41.964
No, um, not that
I recall, no.

13:41.998 --> 13:43.794
Look, now that
this is settled,

13:43.828 --> 13:46.061
maybe you and Glenn can
put this behind you.

13:46.095 --> 13:48.790
No way! How am I supposed
to be friends with someone

13:48.824 --> 13:51.456
who's in love with my wife?
Quagmire is dead to me

13:51.490 --> 13:54.021
and needs to be dealt with
in an appropriate manner.

13:54.056 --> 13:56.086
Shame.

13:56.121 --> 13:57.853
Shame.

13:57.887 --> 13:59.351
Shame.

14:00.550 --> 14:01.884
Shame.

14:01.918 --> 14:04.780
♪ Shame, shame, shame ♪

14:04.814 --> 14:07.845
♪ Shame on you-hoo ♪

14:07.879 --> 14:11.010
♪ Shame, shame, shame ♪

14:11.045 --> 14:12.774
♪ Shame on Q... ♪

14:12.808 --> 14:15.973
This was serious, but it
turned into something fun.

14:21.769 --> 14:24.034
Glenn? Is that you?

14:24.068 --> 14:26.165
Oh, yeah, yeah.
I was just buying a...

14:26.199 --> 14:28.431
a... grocery store cane.

14:28.466 --> 14:29.962
See you, Lois.

14:29.996 --> 14:31.896
Glenn, wait.
Look, if you and Peter

14:31.931 --> 14:35.061
aren't gonna talk this out,
you and I should.

14:35.096 --> 14:36.559
What's there
to talk about?

14:36.593 --> 14:39.058
Everyone knows I'm in love
with my best friend's wife.

14:39.093 --> 14:40.824
It's pathetic.
And humiliating.

14:40.858 --> 14:43.589
Glenn...
I can't trust myself around you.

14:43.623 --> 14:47.118
It's probably best if I...
just never see you again.

14:47.152 --> 14:49.350
Well, you can't just
avoid me forever.

14:49.385 --> 14:51.347
We live on the same street.

14:51.382 --> 14:52.749
Mm.

14:52.783 --> 14:54.180
Well, then...

14:54.214 --> 14:56.813
I know what I have to do.

14:56.847 --> 14:58.644
Good-bye, Lois.

14:58.678 --> 15:01.110
♪ ♪

15:06.605 --> 15:09.237
Oh, sour cream.
You wanted me to remind you.

15:09.272 --> 15:10.602
Sour cream.

15:14.601 --> 15:17.499
Mr. Quagmire, which box
do these beads go in?

15:17.533 --> 15:19.129
Let me smell 'em.

15:19.164 --> 15:21.230
They go in the big box.

15:21.264 --> 15:23.227
Quagmire, I can't
believe you're moving.

15:23.262 --> 15:25.959
Look, give it time--
this whole thing will blow over.

15:25.994 --> 15:27.458
No, it's too awkward.

15:27.492 --> 15:29.625
It's best for everyone
if I just leave.

15:29.659 --> 15:30.890
That's too bad.

15:30.924 --> 15:34.021
We never got to do
that "Joe-Quagmire" lunch.

15:36.785 --> 15:39.150
Well, that'll do it.

15:39.184 --> 15:41.783
Peter, Quagmire's
serious about this.

15:41.817 --> 15:43.880
You got to do something!

15:43.914 --> 15:46.446
You're right.
Quagmire, wait!

15:46.480 --> 15:49.844
You almost left
without this!

15:54.775 --> 15:57.404
You want me to be the one
that says "jiggety" now?

16:03.122 --> 16:05.151
<i>We now return to Dateline.</i>

16:05.387 --> 16:08.068
Our story tonight:
The guy you think did it?

16:08.168 --> 16:09.132
He did it.

16:09.166 --> 16:10.463
Now go to bed.

16:10.498 --> 16:12.464
Your grandkids
are coming tomorrow.

16:16.063 --> 16:19.094
I had a pretty good
egg dish last night.

16:19.129 --> 16:22.456
What? What-what am I supposed
to do with that information?

16:22.491 --> 16:24.989
Well, I don't know.
Maybe ask me for the recipe?

16:25.024 --> 16:26.953
Do you have it?
No.

16:26.987 --> 16:28.986
So what's going on
with you guys?

16:29.021 --> 16:30.651
Nothing much.

16:30.685 --> 16:33.117
See, this is where Quagmire
normally would have told

16:33.151 --> 16:35.147
one of his
outrageous sex stories.

16:35.182 --> 16:38.280
Aw, we don't need him.
I got a sex story for you.

16:38.314 --> 16:40.146
So I'm bangin' this chick,
and she's sayin' to me,

16:40.181 --> 16:42.144
"I'm worried that Chris won't
get into college."

16:42.179 --> 16:43.775
And then I says to her,

16:43.809 --> 16:45.475
"Yeah, that seems
like a legitimate concern."

16:45.509 --> 16:48.341
And then I lost my wood,
and so we just watched Colbert,

16:48.376 --> 16:50.838
and then I took a dump
completely nude.

16:50.872 --> 16:53.037
Who else but Peter?

16:54.770 --> 16:57.401
Peter, face it-- without
Quagmire, we're boring.

16:57.435 --> 16:59.099
Oh, come on,
that ain't true.

16:59.133 --> 17:01.731
Yes, it is. He had
all the fun ideas.

17:01.765 --> 17:04.327
Remember? He even
took me parasailing.

17:06.329 --> 17:08.791
This is awesome!
It's like I'm flying!

17:10.426 --> 17:13.088
I've never felt so alive!

17:13.122 --> 17:16.952
Oh, if only
I had a pair of legs.

17:16.987 --> 17:19.452
All right!

17:22.119 --> 17:24.748
It was the fish part of me
that wanted 'em!

17:30.313 --> 17:34.376
Look, Peter, I'm
sorry Quagmire moved away,

17:34.410 --> 17:37.306
but you can't just sit around
the house and drink all day.

17:37.341 --> 17:39.639
It's all your fault
Quagmire fell in love with you.

17:39.673 --> 17:41.768
Traipsin' around
in your tan pants

17:41.803 --> 17:44.368
and your green shirt
and your soothing voice.

17:44.402 --> 17:45.933
<i>My fault?!</i>

17:45.968 --> 17:47.700
Yeah, everything is messed up.

17:47.734 --> 17:50.296
I lost my best friend,
my buddies are all fighting,

17:50.331 --> 17:52.863
that chick at work is saying
stuff that ain't true.

17:52.897 --> 17:54.293
Okay, you know what?

17:54.328 --> 17:55.795
Enough feeling
sorry for yourself.

17:55.829 --> 17:57.925
We're fixing this now.
Get in the car.

17:57.960 --> 17:59.759
What? Why?
You'll see.

17:59.794 --> 18:01.756
Why should I trust you?

18:01.790 --> 18:04.288
You're always trickin' me into
going places I don't want to.

18:04.323 --> 18:08.220
Oh... you said we were going
to a place Walt Disney built.

18:08.254 --> 18:10.716
No, Peter. I said supported.

18:15.983 --> 18:18.612
<i>By the way,
don't go on the train ride.</i>

18:23.209 --> 18:25.075
I've been playing
a game I invented

18:25.110 --> 18:27.771
called "mini racquetball"
in your garage.

18:27.805 --> 18:29.938
Uh-huh.
It's pretty fun.

18:29.972 --> 18:31.769
He has not won
a single point.

18:31.802 --> 18:33.836
You don't have to win
to have fun.

18:36.566 --> 18:40.230
Lois? Peter. Zod.

18:40.263 --> 18:42.995
Hey. You're parked behind
my trapezoid-thing.

18:43.030 --> 18:45.162
Yeah, yeah,
I'll move it in a sec.

18:45.197 --> 18:47.991
Glenn, all this nonsense
has to stop now.

18:48.026 --> 18:50.225
The only reason
this became an issue is because

18:50.258 --> 18:52.255
Peter heard something
he wasn't supposed to hear.

18:52.290 --> 18:54.089
<i>Guy from Superman
lives here?!</i>

18:54.123 --> 18:56.319
And the truth is,
we all have private thoughts

18:56.353 --> 18:59.318
we don't act on,
and that's okay.

18:59.351 --> 19:01.415
For instance, every time
I'm on the subway,

19:01.450 --> 19:03.582
I want to push a stranger
onto the tracks.

19:03.616 --> 19:04.647
And that's fine!

19:04.681 --> 19:06.314
I don't do it!

19:06.348 --> 19:08.012
I guess you're right.

19:08.046 --> 19:10.378
<i>I don't totally disagree with
what Kim Jong-un's doing,</i>

19:10.412 --> 19:12.209
but you don't see
me moving there.

19:12.243 --> 19:14.173
I take medicine
I get from the veterinarian.

19:14.207 --> 19:15.574
Is that one?

19:15.607 --> 19:17.504
No, no, it's not,
but the point is,

19:17.539 --> 19:19.471
we all have secret thoughts.

19:19.505 --> 19:22.034
But there's no reason they
should ruin our friendships.

19:22.069 --> 19:24.002
Sometimes I think about
going to the hospital

19:24.036 --> 19:25.533
and switching
the babies around.

19:25.567 --> 19:27.367
Somali pirates
seem cool, too.

19:27.401 --> 19:29.730
I wouldn't mind eating
the Phillie Phanatic.

19:29.764 --> 19:32.163
See? We're all
terrible people inside.

19:32.197 --> 19:34.559
Joe's a little worse
than the rest of us,

19:34.593 --> 19:37.792
but we all just shove
our thoughts deep down,

19:37.825 --> 19:39.359
where they can't
hurt anybody.

19:39.392 --> 19:41.888
Huh, maybe you're right.

19:41.922 --> 19:43.656
Of course I'm right.

19:43.690 --> 19:46.485
The secret to happiness is
burying all your true feelings

19:46.520 --> 19:49.351
and living a life
of bland compromise.

19:49.385 --> 19:51.481
So here's the question, Glenn.

19:51.516 --> 19:55.545
Do you love Peter enough
to repress your love for me?

19:59.576 --> 20:02.840
Peter, if you're willing
to forget all about this,

20:02.875 --> 20:06.472
I'm more than happy to continue
hiding my true feelings.

20:06.507 --> 20:08.606
I do miss us
hanging out together.

20:08.640 --> 20:11.269
Huh. Sorry I kind of
went a little crazy.

20:11.302 --> 20:13.368
Ah, that's all right.

20:13.403 --> 20:15.831
And I'm sorry
I will always love your wife.

20:15.866 --> 20:17.299
Which I don't.

20:17.334 --> 20:18.765
Thank you, Glenn.

20:18.798 --> 20:19.629
All right!

20:19.663 --> 20:21.197
What do you say
we all celebrate

20:21.232 --> 20:23.594
with a game
of mini racquetball?

20:23.628 --> 20:25.993
Wait. Is mini racquetball
just Ping-Pong?

20:26.028 --> 20:28.723
Kind of.

20:32.288 --> 20:34.987
Boy, it's good to have the gang
together again.

20:35.022 --> 20:36.817
Yeah, welcome
home, buddy.

20:36.852 --> 20:39.283
Man, I missed sitting around,
just shooting the breeze.

20:39.318 --> 20:41.281
Hey, so how'd you get
your house back?

20:41.316 --> 20:42.782
This ought to be good.

20:42.816 --> 20:44.246
I suspended escrow.

20:44.280 --> 20:45.511
Oh.

20:46.813 --> 20:49.268
Hey, guys, you know that egg
dish I was talking about?

20:49.367 --> 20:52.270
Turns out that was
just a dream I had.

20:52.271 --> 20:58.762
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru